# Forms — react-hook-form + FormProvider

Every form UI must use **react-hook-form**. Wrap the form tree in **`FormProvider`** and use shared **`Ct*`** field components from `@/modules/app/components/forms` (Ant Design + `Controller` + `useFormContext`).

## Required

- `useForm<FormValues>()` in the page, hook, or `Ct{Name}Form` — typed `FormValues` in `types/`
- `<FormProvider {...form}>` around all fields (spread the full `UseFormReturn`)
- Field components: `CtTextInput`, `CtTextArea`, `CtSelect`, `CtRadio` — **never** pass `control` into individual fields
- Custom or one-off inputs: `useFormContext()` + `Controller` in the same file (same pattern as `Ct*` fields)
- Submit via `form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)` on a native `<form>`

## Example

```tsx
import { FormProvider, useForm } from 'react-hook-form'
import { Button } from 'antd'
import { CtTextInput, CtTextArea, CtSelect } from '@/modules/app/components/forms'
import type { BookFormValues } from '@/modules/book/types/book.types'

export function CtBookForm({ onSubmit }: { onSubmit: (values: BookFormValues) => void }) {
  const form = useForm<BookFormValues>({ defaultValues: { title: '', author: '' } })

  return (
    <FormProvider {...form}>
      <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className="flex max-w-lg flex-col gap-4">
        <CtTextInput<BookFormValues>
          name="title"
          label="Title"
          rules={{ required: true }}
        />
        <CtTextArea<BookFormValues> name="description" label="Description" rows={4} />
        <CtSelect<BookFormValues>
          name="status"
          label="Status"
          options={[
            { value: 'draft', label: 'Draft' },
            { value: 'published', label: 'Published' },
          ]}
        />
        <Button type="primary" htmlType="submit">
          Save
        </Button>
      </form>
    </FormProvider>
  )
}
```

Hook-owned form (upsert pattern): return `form` from the hook; the page or `Ct{Name}Form` wraps children in `<FormProvider {...form}>`.

```tsx
const { form, onSubmit, isPending } = useBookUpsertForm(bookId)

return (
  <FormProvider {...form}>
    <form onSubmit={onSubmit}>…</form>
  </FormProvider>
)
```

## Field components (`modules/app/components/forms/`)

| Component | Ant Design | Props |
|-----------|------------|-------|
| `CtTextInput` | `Input` | `name`, `label?`, `rules?`, + `InputProps` |
| `CtTextArea` | `Input.TextArea` | `name`, `label?`, `rules?`, + `TextAreaProps` |
| `CtSelect` | `Select` | `name`, `label?`, `rules?`, + `SelectProps` |
| `CtRadio` | `Radio.Group` | `name`, `label?`, `rules?`, + `RadioGroupProps` |

Pass the form generic for typed `name`: `CtTextInput<BookFormValues> name="title"`.

## Do not

- Use raw `useState` for multi-field form state
- Pass `control` prop into field components — use `FormProvider` context
- Inline `Controller` + Ant Design in feature forms when a `Ct*` component fits
- Use Formik, Final Form, or Ant Design `Form` alone without `react-hook-form`
- Use Ant Design `Form.Item` for validation (RHF `rules` on `Ct*` / `Controller` instead)
